      "mechanism": "At cycle 13, rst=1 triggers the write-domain reset. The original code resets only wr_ptr, leaving wr_ptr_cur and drop_frame uninitialized. The discovery trace shows drop_frame=1 at cycles 13-14 instead of expected 0. This patch adds explicit resets for drop_frame and wr_ptr_cur inside the write-domain reset block (line 99), ensuring both packet-state bits are cleared on reset alongside wr_ptr. Cited failure: drop_frame=1 at cycle 13 (expected 0)."
