    {
      "id": "patch_15a85deae41e",
      "failure_port": "drop_frame",
      "source_line": 99,
      "mechanism": "Same write-domain reset block as above. The original code omits wr_ptr_cur reset; the testbench expects wr_ptr_cur=0 after reset so that subsequent frame writes use the correct base pointer. Resetting wr_ptr_cur here (line 99) aligns the commit pointer with the committed pointer on reset, preventing spurious drop_frame assertions caused by a stale wr_ptr_cur. Cited failure: drop_frame=1 at cycle 13 (expected 0)."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_9d300784e043",
      "failure_port": "drop_frame",
      "source_line": 99,
      "mechanism": "Minimal version of the same fix: only adds drop_frame <= 0 in the write-domain reset (line 99). The discovery trace shows drop_frame stuck at 1 after reset; clearing it here directly matches the expected 0 at cycles 13-14. Cited failure: drop_frame=1 at cycle 13 (expected 0)."
